<title>CANADA: Quebec liquor outlets workers threaten strike.</title>
<headline>Quebec liquor outlets workers threaten strike.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union representing 2,500 employees at Quebec government liquor outlets voted 73 percent in favour of giving a strike mandate to its contract negotiating committee.</p>
<p>Negotiations between the Societe des alcools du Quebec (SAQ) and the unionized liquor outlet workers continue with the aid of a government mediator.</p>
<p>A union representative said the major point of contention is the SAQ's use of non-unionized staff to do the work traditionally done by unionized employees.</p>
<p>If negotiations fail, the liquor outlet workers could go on strike during the busy Christmas holiday season, the union said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Montreal bureau (514) 985-2434</p>
</text>
